        IOUtils.closeQuietly(reader);
    }
    reader = null;
}
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that when the end-of-input is reached (`line` is `null`), the `closeResources()` method is called to properly close the `reader`, preventing resource leaks. This change ensures that all resources are correctly cleaned up before returning `null`, allowing the `LineEntityProcessor` to handle multiple files correctly in conjunction with `FileListEntityProcessor`.

